-- title:
--   Irrelevant ideal is contained in the image ideal under degreewise spanning
-- statement:
--   Let $S$ and $S'$ be commutative rings, let $R$ be a commutative $S$-algebra equipped with a family of $S$-submodules $\mathcal{R} : \mathbb{N} \to \mathrm{Submodule}\,S\,R$ making $R$ an $\mathbb{N}$-graded $S$-algebra, and let $R'$ be a commutative $S'$-algebra with an $\mathbb{N}$-grading $\mathcal{R}'$ by $S'$-submodules. Let $\vartheta : R \to R'$ be a ring homomorphism which is degreewise compatible with the gradings, that is $\vartheta(x) \in \mathcal{R}'_n$ whenever $x \in \mathcal{R}_n$, and assume that for every $n > 0$ the component $\mathcal{R}'_n$ is contained in the $S'$-submodule of $R'$ spanned by the set $\vartheta(\mathcal{R}_n)$. Then, viewing $\vartheta$ together with its degreewise compatibility as a graded ring homomorphism $\mathcal{R} \to \mathcal{R}'$, the irrelevant homogeneous ideal of $\mathcal{R}'$ (the homogeneous ideal of elements whose degree-$0$ component vanishes) is contained in the pushforward along that graded homomorphism of the irrelevant homogeneous ideal of $\mathcal{R}$; the inequality is an inclusion of the underlying ideals of $R'$. No compatibility between the base rings $S$ and $S'$ is required.
--
--   This is the standard hypothesis, going back to EGA II 2.8.1, under which a graded ring homomorphism induces a morphism $\operatorname{Proj} R' \to \operatorname{Proj} R$: the irrelevant ideal of the target grading must be generated by the image of the irrelevant ideal of the source. It is used here to supply that hypothesis in the construction of descent data for $\operatorname{Proj}$ along a faithfully flat base change, as required by [`AlgebraicGeometry.exists_descent_of_faithfullyFlat_of_cocycle`](thm.html#AlgebraicGeometry.exists_descent_of_faithfullyFlat_of_cocycle).
-- source:
